(3979504, 564446, 57032, '<td valign="top">Hi from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>First of all, congratulations on your top 20 finish. This image has excellent composition, although I agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=43774" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">KarenNfld</a> that a bit of the sky could have been cropped out (though not too much, since the negative space serves a useful purpose here). The clouds are beautiful and perfectly exposed, in my opinion; they flow nicely, and take on a great colour from the lights below.<br/> <br/>As for the lights below, I''d agree with <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/31.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=36283" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">jaymody</a> that they''re a bit overexposed. Considering this challenge called for basic editing, however, I think you did a great job of balancing priorities.<br/> <br/>Finally, I have to say that the water was captured perfectly. Great clarity, and beautiful reflections.<br/> <br/>Certainly worthy of a top 20 finish. Great shot.<br/> <br/>Geoff<br/> <br/>(Edit to fix username link.)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-08-08 01:34:54.</i></td>', 'Hi from the Critique Club, First of all, congratulations on your top 20 finish. This image has excellent composition, although I agree with  KarenNfld that a bit of the sky could have been cropped out (though not too much, since the negative space serves a useful purpose here). The clouds are beautiful and perfectly exposed, in my opinion; they flow nicely, and take on a great colour from the lights below. As for the lights below, I''d agree with  jaymody that they''re a bit overexposed. Considering this challenge called for basic editing, however, I think you did a great job of balancing priorities. Finally, I have to say that the water was captured perfectly. Great clarity, and beautiful reflections. Certainly worthy of a top 20 finish. Great shot. Geoff (Edit to fix username link.)', '2007-08-08 02:34:00.000000', '2007-08-08 02:34:54.000000', 0),
(3979510, 564434, 18197, '<td valign="top">I like the centered (side to side) aspect of the photo but might have moved the subject down a bit. There is nice detail in the spider, but the focus is a little soft to bring it out. Also, possibly if the spider filled the frame, it might have been easier to appreciate the detail. You might have to move closer to the subject to pull this off - zooming in in an editing program may make the softness worse. Another approach might be to reduce the zoom and show the spider hanging from a web thread and located according to the rule of thirds. The simple background certainly emphasizes the subject. I wonder if a nice bokeh background might have increased the interest level of the photo. Good luck in future challenges.</td>', 'I like the centered (side to side) aspect of the photo but might have moved the subject down a bit. There is nice detail in the spider, but the focus is a little soft to bring it out. Also, possibly if the spider filled the frame, it might have been easier to appreciate the detail. You might have to move closer to the subject to pull this off - zooming in in an editing program may make the softness worse. Another approach might be to reduce the zoom and show the spider hanging from a web thread and located according to the rule of thirds. The simple background certainly emphasizes the subject. I wonder if a nice bokeh background might have increased the interest level of the photo. Good luck in future challenges.', '2007-08-08 02:35:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(3979548, 563726, 78303, '<td valign="top">This barn will be gone in less than 6 months, I have been told.  THere is going to be a bypass road built to feed into the neighborhood behind it that is being built up.  It is sad to see such reminders of our past plowed under and paved over.  So, we better photograph them while we can!<br/></td>', 'This barn will be gone in less than 6 months, I have been told.  THere is going to be a bypass road built to feed into the neighborhood behind it that is being built up.  It is sad to see such reminders of our past plowed under and paved over.  So, we better photograph them while we can!', '2007-08-08 02:43:55.000000', NULL, 0),
